1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,400
Your own repositories.

2
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:03,840
Shared projects.

3
00:00:04,540 --> 00:00:05,820
Libraries you starred for later.

4
00:00:06,760 --> 00:00:07,460
Finding them is easy.

5
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:09,940
Remembering how they fit together is harder.

6
00:00:10,940 --> 00:00:13,640
GitHub Manager brings them into one workspace, where you

7
00:00:13,640 --> 00:00:15,620
can search, explore, and organize.

8
00:00:17,162 --> 00:00:18,642
Projects group an initiative.

9
00:00:19,682 --> 00:00:20,762
Domains group those projects.

10
00:00:21,622 --> 00:00:25,102
Topics describe capabilities, and tags describe technologies.

11
00:00:26,042 --> 00:00:29,382
Two repositories can both use Python without belonging to

12
00:00:29,382 --> 00:00:30,122
the same project.

13
00:00:30,682 --> 00:00:33,022
There are two separate AI jobs.

14
00:00:33,862 --> 00:00:36,902
Taxonomy discovery proposes a vocabulary from a collection

15
00:00:36,902 --> 00:00:37,702
of repositories.

16
00:00:38,402 --> 00:00:39,742
You review and edit it.

17
00:00:40,162 --> 00:00:43,182
Classification then works with approved concepts, rather

18
00:00:43,182 --> 00:00:44,422
than inventing new labels.

19
00:00:46,462 --> 00:00:48,162
Follow our synthetic Orion example.

20
00:00:48,802 --> 00:00:52,482
Its README says: patient intake API for the Orion

21
00:00:52,482 --> 00:00:53,402
Clinical Platform.

22
00:00:53,402 --> 00:00:56,042
Uses FastAPI and Python.

23
00:00:56,042 --> 00:00:59,922
We keep that purpose sentence, its evidence reference, and

24
00:00:59,922 --> 00:01:00,642
useful phrases.

25
00:01:02,194 --> 00:01:04,234
Local search retrieves six possible concepts.

26
00:01:04,974 --> 00:01:08,234
Some are distractions: Forge shares the word platform, but

27
00:01:08,234 --> 00:01:09,734
that doesn't establish a relationship.

28
00:01:10,634 --> 00:01:11,934
Retrieval finds possibilities.

29
00:01:12,554 --> 00:01:13,534
It doesn't assign them.

30
00:01:14,670 --> 00:01:17,910
The model receives evidence, candidate definitions, instructions,

31
00:01:18,010 --> 00:01:19,170
and a response schema.

32
00:01:19,730 --> 00:01:23,730
In the saved test, it selected Orion, Web APIs,

33
00:01:24,590 --> 00:01:27,710
FastAPI, and Python, citing the purpose sentence.

34
00:01:28,270 --> 00:01:30,970
You review those suggestions before accepting them.

35
00:01:32,262 --> 00:01:35,002
The app remembers completed analysis separately from labels.

36
00:01:36,042 --> 00:01:37,722
Removing a project doesn't erase that receipt.

37
00:01:38,702 --> 00:01:40,322
Later changes can reconcile locally.

38
00:01:40,942 --> 00:01:43,482
A fresh AI analysis remains an explicit choice.

39
00:01:44,890 --> 00:01:49,710
Every model call has a reviewed budget: count, reserve,

40
00:01:50,730 --> 00:01:51,710
generate, record.

41
00:01:52,850 --> 00:01:54,330
Find the repository you need.

42
00:01:55,510 --> 00:01:56,490
Understand why it belongs.

43
00:01:57,390 --> 00:01:59,190
Keep the final decision yours.
